{"id":"000W5C","title":"No Two Dominoes Alike","author":"gk122","solvedCount":2,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-21T11:18:12+00:00","posted":"Heute, 09:57 Uhr","rules":"Short version of the rules\n\nNormal sudoku with standard clues, except that no two clued dominoes may contain the same pair of digits.\n\nLong version of the rules\n\nNormal sudoku rules apply.\n\nNo two dominoes alike: a domino is a pair of orthogonally adjacent cells. No two dominoes marked with a clue may contain the same two digits, in either order, whatever the clues are. For example, if a white dot joins an 8 and a 9, no other clued domino (not even an inequality sign) can contain 8 and 9.\n\nClues: all clues are standard.\n\n• Digits joined by a white dot are consecutive.\n\n• Digits joined by a black dot are in a 1:2 ratio (one is double the other).\n\n• Digits joined by an X sum to 10; by a V, to 5.\n\n• Inequality signs point to the smaller digit.\n\nX and V are drawn inside circles to make them easy to tell apart from inequality signs.\n\nPlay on SudokuPad","solutionCode":"Row 5","tags":["Sudoku","Greater Than (Variante)","XV (Variante)","Kropki Pairs (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/883kqc6l7m","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/883kqc6l7m","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-21T11:18:12+00:00"}